<!-- @before Conflict UX :: guide -->
### Read protection and write protection differ

Rejecting an older response protects the screen’s observed order. It does not stop a stale edit overwriting a newer server value. Submit the base revision and require an atomic precondition check, such as [HTTP If-Match](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110.html#section-13.1.1). The feature still needs an explicit conflict outcome.

<!-- @before Offline and Reset Contracts :: staff -->
### Reset the continuation, preserve the user’s work

An expired cursor can require a new snapshot without authorizing deletion of pending edits. Define snapshot scope, tombstones and outbox replay together. The same [session guarantee](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/courses/cs734/2000FA/cached%20papers/SessionGuaranteesPDIS_1.html) must remain meaningful after reconnect.
